    Your job (5 steps to hardening):
    
    Step 1: Resilience Patterns (5/5 required)
    ├─ Timeout: 5s default (configurable per endpoint)
    ├─ Retry: max 3 attempts, exponential backoff
    ├─ Circuit Breaker: 50% error threshold, 30s wait
    ├─ Bulkhead: max 10 concurrent calls
    ├─ Idempotency: UUID header on every request
    └─ Add: resilience4j annotations + config
    
    Step 2: Security Controls (6/6 required)
    ├─ AuthN/AuthZ: TLS + certificate pinning
    ├─ Least Privilege: service can only access its own data
    ├─ Secrets: all credentials in vault (no hardcoding)
    ├─ Input Validation: null/blank checks at seam
    ├─ Error Handling: generic error messages (no info disclosure)
    └─ Audit Logging: log all access with user context
    
    Step 3: Observability (3/3 required)
    ├─ Tracing: trace ID propagation through seam
    ├─ Metrics: export via Micrometer (circuit breaker, retry, latency)
    └─ Alerts: error rate > 1%, p95 > 500ms triggers alert
    
    Step 4: Progressive Cutover Plan (4 stages required)
    ├─ Stage 1: 5% canary traffic (10+ min monitoring)
    ├─ Stage 2: 25% (10+ min monitoring)
    ├─ Stage 3: 50% (10+ min monitoring)
